# What Linguist counts, and what it should not.
#
# GitHub reported this repository as 57.8% HTML and 39.5% TypeScript,
# which is a false description of what somebody is buying. The product is
# a Next.js application in strict TypeScript; the HTML is 6.8 MB of
# machine output that happens to be tracked.
#
# Measured, rather than guessed: 89.4% of every tracked HTML byte is
# `landing/demo/`, the static export of the running app, about which
# `scripts/export-demo.ts` says in its own header, "Nothing in this
# directory is written by hand." Another 2.4% is `landing/docs/`, the
# published copies of this repository's own markdown. Marking those two as
# generated leaves the hand-written marketing pages counted, which is
# correct, because a person did write them.
#
# The second effect is worth as much as the first: a demo re-export churns
# 38 files, and a generated file is collapsed in a diff instead of burying
# the change somebody actually needs to read.

landing/demo/** linguist-generated=true
landing/docs/*.html linguist-generated=true

# Fonts and captures are binary, and a diff of them helps nobody.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
